Subject: [PATCH] Remove disable of a pass absent from pinned OpenVINO 2026.2

This packaging patch applies only to the sealed OpenVINO 2026.2.0 source
52ddc07385712456dd9f8c5ecf05d7e49c6da329. Its transpose_sinking.hpp neither
declares TransposeFQ nor registers it in TransposeSinking. The compiler's
validation/openvino_config.json instead names revision
4089686065a245d648cdd2b99c31884f53cb7a5e, which contains that pass.
Remove the obsolete disable call; do not replace it with TransposeFQReduction
or TransposeFuse, which are distinct passes and remain unchanged.
Reference: https://github.com/openvinotoolkit/openvino/blob/52ddc07385712456dd9f8c5ecf05d7e49c6da329/src/common/transformations/include/transformations/common_optimizations/transpose_sinking.hpp
Reference: https://github.com/openvinotoolkit/openvino/blob/4089686065a245d648cdd2b99c31884f53cb7a5e/src/common/transformations/include/transformations/common_optimizations/transpose_sinking.hpp

Regression: check-compatibility.py compiles the actual affected translation
units with their generated release flags. Original units fail in the retained
September 7 diagnostic build. No warning option is changed.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/frontend/IE.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/frontend/IE.cpp
@@ -5844,7 +5844,6 @@
     pass_config->disable<ov::pass::FakeQuantizeMulFusion>();
     pass_config->disable<ov::pass::MulFakeQuantizeFusion>();
     pass_config->disable<ov::pass::MultiplyConvolutionFusion>();
-    pass_config->disable<ov::pass::TransposeFQ>();
 
     // NMS conversion passes
     manager.register_pass<ov::pass::ConvertNMS1ToNMS9>();
